+# Daily Grind browser tools
+
+The static homepage loads `app.js`, which registers three client-side WebMCP tools:
+
+- `get_seasonal_menu({ query?: string })`: read the displayed Seasonal Favorites menu, optionally searching names and descriptions.
+- `select_drink({ drinkId: string })`: highlight a drink, select it in the order form, and reveal the form.
+- `order_drink({ drinkId: string, quantity?: integer })`: add 1–10 drinks (default 1) to the visible demo order.
+
+Drink IDs are `maple-oat-latte`, `dark-roast-espresso`, and `cold-brew`.
+Tools return MCP-style text content containing JSON; invalid arguments return `isError: true` with a useful message and do not change the page. Orders exist only in page memory, reset on reload, and never submit a payment or real café order. Buttons and the order form use the same actions as the tools.
+
+Native discovery uses `document.modelContext.registerTool`, with compatibility for `navigator.modelContext.registerTool`. See the [Chrome WebMCP documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/webmcp/agentic-javascript-tools). Unsupported browsers keep the normal UI and expose the same tool schemas and handlers through this fallback:
+
+```js
+window.dailyGrind.listTools();
+await window.dailyGrind.callTool('get_seasonal_menu', { query: 'oat' });
+await window.dailyGrind.callTool('select_drink', { drinkId: 'cold-brew' });
+await window.dailyGrind.callTool('order_drink', { drinkId: 'cold-brew', quantity: 2 });
+```
+
+Run non-browser checks with `node --test tests/app.test.cjs`. No dependencies or build step are required.
